Project: Ticket Booking & Reservation System (Spring Boot 3 + Java 22 + PostgreSQL + React)

Environment & Build Rules:
- Always include Maven Wrapper files (mvnw, mvnw.cmd, .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties) so the project builds via .\mvnw without requiring a global Maven installation.
- Target Java 21 bytecode compatibility in pom.xml (compatible with local JDK 22).

Backend Architecture Rules:
- Use constructor injection everywhere (no field @Autowired).
- Separate persistence entities from request/response DTOs (use Java records for DTOs).
- Use Bean Validation (@Valid) on all controller inputs and handle all errors via a central @RestControllerAdvice returning structured JSON error responses.
- Keep @Transactional boundaries strictly in the service layer, never on controllers.
- Add concise comments explaining concurrency locking, deadlock prevention, and hold expiration logic.

Frontend Rules:
- React + TypeScript (Vite) in a /frontend directory with modular API client services.
- Clean, light-themed, responsive UI.